module lib/basis/named
  A basis set by its name, as PySCF spells it: `basis_named("6-31G*")` returns
  the `Basis` record of the table in lib/basis that PySCF would load for that
  name. Names PySCF treats as one set (`6-31G*`, `631gs`) give the same
  table. It looks among the tables the program uses, and loads all eight
  only for a program that uses none.

basis_key  @14fb63c2
  why   PySCF compares basis names after this same normalization, so any
        spelling PySCF accepts for these sets is accepted here.
  name  the basis name as a person wrote it

basis_module  @0d527973
  why   A name whose table the program does not use stops the run with the
        import line that would load it; this is where that line comes from.
  k     a normalized key, as `basis_key` gives it

basis_named  @0c09b687
  why   lib/hf/mole takes the basis as a name, the way PySCF's `gto.M` does.
        A name with no table here stops the run and lists the names that
        have one, instead of falling back to some other set; a name whose
        table the program does not use stops it and names the module to use.
  name  the basis name as written
  k     its normalized key, compared with the keys of the tables the program uses
  m     the module of the table the key names, `""` when no table has it
